  "connector": "〜な",
  "gloss": "な-adjectives: quiet, handy, liked",
  "title": "〜な — な-adjectives",
  "pattern": "〜な + noun / 〜です / 〜じゃないです / 〜でした",
  "explanation": "Some describing words take な before a noun: {静|しず}かな{町|まち} — a quiet town; {便利|べんり}な{店|みせ} — a handy shop. At the end of a sentence they act like nouns: {静|しず}かです, {静|しず}かじゃないです, {静|しず}かでした. {好|す}き, {嫌|きら}い, {元気|げんき}, {暇|ひま} and きれい are all な-adjectives, きれい included, though it ends in い.",
  "natural": "{好|す}きな{食|た}べ{物|もの}は{何|なん}ですか — what’s your favourite food? — is a classic first-conversation question.",
  "stiff": "No な at the end: {静|しず}かなです is wrong. And きれい isn’t an い-adjective: “not pretty” is きれいじゃない, never きれくない.",
